# C0 Operator vs Agent — Non-Negotiable

## Rob (dashboard only)

- Picks content, composes, generates (script, HeyGen, cold open approval)
- Reviews everything the pipeline exposes for creative/QA sign-off
- **Only Rob hits Approve and Publish** in the job queue

## Agent (terminals only)

- Fix code when assembly output does not match creative direction
- Reassemble when needed (after deploy, when no job ffmpeg is running)
- Deploy via `bash scripts/deploy_c0.sh` **only when `pgrep -f tmp/asm_` is empty**
- Serena QA on commits, Jira + Confluence updates per workflow rules

## Agent MUST NOT

- Call `POST /job/:id/run-gate5`, `POST /publish`, `POST /job/:id/advance` to Gate 5, or any upload path
- Use `forcePublish: true` or bypass operator creative guards
- Ask Rob whether workflow requirements apply — they are requirements
- Restart pm2 / deploy while assembly ffmpeg is running

## Agent success criteria

Assembly output matches creative spec (bookends, laughs, credits, chrome, script). If not → fix code → deploy when idle → reassemble → Rob reviews again.
